  "title": "Erdős Problem #610",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "For a graph $G$ let $\\tau(G)$ denote the minimal number of vertices that include at least one from each maximal clique of $G$ (sometimes called the clique transversal number).\nEstimate $\\tau(G)$. In particular, is it true that if $G$ has $n$ vertices then $ \\tau(G) \\leq n-\\omega(n)\\sqrt{n} $ for some $\\omega(n)\\to \\infty$, or even $ \\tau(G) \\leq n-c\\sqrt{n\\log n} $ for some absolute constant $c>0$?",
